    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A more general approach to regression analysis expresses the covariance matrix of the vector of residuals as $ \\sigma_e^2 \\mathbf{R} $, with $ \\sigma(e_i, e_j) = R_{ij} \\sigma_e^2 $. Lack of independence between residuals is indicated by the presence of nonzero off-diagonal elements in $ \\mathbf{R} $, while heteroscedasticity is indicated by differences in the diagonal elements of $ \\mathbf{R} $. Generalized (or weighted) least squares (GLS) takes these complications into account. As shown in Appendix 3, if the linear model is",
